PATCH 283: the landing-gear state method FUN_0000_ad3b + the per-object-type STATE-CHANGE dispatch
FUN_0000_a19e -- DGROUP near-offset base-loss (SIGSEGV), reached from the object animation update ab03.

ASM-verified (asm 0xad3b-0xad61, 0xa19e-0xa1a6; DS=DGROUP=0x1c00): di=object near offset.  ad3b toggles
the gear-state byte[di+0x90] via a19e when altitude word[di+0x34] crosses 0xe00; Ghidra host-ptr-deref'd
param_1 + read [di+0x34] as a 32-bit int (asm WORD).  a19e dispatches a type-specific method
word[DG:(word[di]*2-0x69a2)] with DI live; Ghidra deref'd *param_1 host-ptr + dropped the object arg --
its targets (a1a7 etc.) read the object as a HOST POINTER, so it now passes g_mem+0x1c000+di.  Both
rebased to the DGROUP model.  (a19e's al gear-direction selector is dropped through its 1-param sig:
gear-state only, non-crashing.)  Mission-cascade only.
--- a/fist.c
+++ b/fist.c
@@ -26145,7 +26145,15 @@
 void __allregs FUN_0000_a19e(int *param_1)
 
 {
-  (*(code *)fist_icall_near(0x0u,(uint16_t)(*(undefined2 *)(*param_1 * 2 + -0x69a2))))();
+  /* PATCH 283: the per-object-type STATE-CHANGE method dispatch (asm 0xa19e-0xa1a6; DS=DGROUP=0x1c00).
+   * di=object near offset in param_1; asm `mov bx,[di]; shl bx,1; call [bx-0x69a2]` selects a type-
+   * specific method from word[DG:(word[di]*2-0x69a2)] and calls it with DI live.  Ghidra deref'd
+   * *param_1 as a host pointer (SIGSEGV) and dropped the object arg.  The dispatch targets (a1a7 etc.)
+   * read the object as a HOST POINTER, so pass g_mem+0x1c000+di. */
+  unsigned char *dg = (unsigned char *)g_mem + 0x1c000;
+  unsigned int di = (unsigned short)(uintptr_t)param_1;
+  uint16_t vec = *(uint16_t *)(dg + (unsigned short)((unsigned short)(*(uint16_t *)(dg + di) << 1) - 0x69a2));
+  (*(code *)fist_icall_near(0x0u,vec))((int)(intptr_t)(dg + di));
   return;
 }
 
@@ -27888,16 +27896,23 @@
